### According to India's official trade data, what was the total value of India's imports from China during the period April to August 2019?
Answer: According to the official data cited, India's imports from China during April-August 2019 were approximately $29.82 billion, calculated from the reported 27.63% decline to $21.58 billion in the 2020 period.

Source URL: https://www.businesstoday.in/current/economy-politics/imports-from-china-decline-by-27-63-during-april-august-2020-piyush-goyal/story/416674.html

### Based on the official figures for April-August 2020 and April-August 2019, what is the exact percentage increase in India's imports from China between these two periods?
Answer: Based on official figures provided by India's Commerce and Industry Minister in Parliament, India's imports from China decreased by 27.63% during April-August 2020 compared to the same period in 2019, rather than increasing as claimed. As cited from the source, "India's imports from China declined by 27.63 per cent during April-August this fiscal to $21.58 billion over the same period previous year."

Source URL: https://www.businesstoday.in/current/economy-politics/imports-from-china-decline-by-27-63-during-april-august-2020-piyush-goyal/story/416674.html

### Is the 27% figure cited in the claim an exact calculation or a rounded approximation of the actual percentage change?
Answer: The 27% figure cited in the claim is a rounded approximation of the actual percentage change, as the official data provided to Parliament states the decline was "27.63 per cent."

