## Final Judgement
The fact-check reveals a clear contradiction between the claim and official Indian government data. According to India's Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal in Parliament, imports from China during April–August 2020 actually declined by 27.63% to $21.58 billion, down from approximately $29.82 billion in the same period of 2019. The 27% figure in the claim is a rounded approximation of this decline, not an increase.

No further information is needed, as the recorded evidence provides explicit, official figures that directly oppose the claim's assertion.

